[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Software Requirements Data
PREFIX: HLR-

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Verifier Component Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-001
TITLE: Execution Log Loading
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier shall load execution logs from JSON files and parse them into in-memory
structures for comparison against test case definitions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-002
TITLE: Output Pattern Matching
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier shall compare actual output against expected patterns using exact match,
regex match, and JSON schema validation strategies.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-003
TITLE: Exit Code Verification
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier shall verify step exit codes match expected values with optional range
or set matching.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-004
TITLE: Detailed Mismatch Reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
When verification fails, the verifier shall report expected vs actual values with
character-level highlighting of differences.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-005
TITLE: Batch Verification Orchestration
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier shall orchestrate verification of multiple execution logs with aggregated
pass/fail counts and summary statistics.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Test Case Content Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TC-001
TITLE: Test Case Parsing
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall parse test case YAML files extracting test_case_id, title,
sequences, steps, and metadata fields.
<<<
