TITLE: Help and Version Support
STATEMENT: >>>
All executables shall provide comprehensive help via --help and semantic versioning
via --version.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-INT-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PERF-001
TITLE: Streaming and Memory Efficiency
STATEMENT: >>>
Large file handling shall use streaming readers to process content in chunks rather
than loading entire files into memory.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-PERF-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PERF-002
TITLE: Parallel Processing Optimization
STATEMENT: >>>
Parallel execution shall minimize synchronization overhead and implement dynamic load
balancing strategies.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-PERF-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PERF-003
TITLE: Incremental Compilation Caching
STATEMENT: >>>
Build system shall leverage incremental compilation caching for faster builds and
dependency-based rebuild optimization.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-PERF-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-REL-001
TITLE: Graceful Error Handling Implementation
STATEMENT: >>>
All components shall implement comprehensive try-catch blocks and return descriptive
error messages.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-REL-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-REL-002
TITLE: Atomic File Write Operations
STATEMENT: >>>
File write operations shall use atomic patterns: write to temporary file, then rename
to target to ensure consistency.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-REL-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-REL-003
TITLE: Timeout and Resource Management
STATEMENT: >>>
Long-running operations shall implement timeout handlers with proper cleanup of files,
processes, and memory.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-REL-003

